$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of 22 (3.00 g, 9.23 mmol) and aldehyde 16 (2.16 g, 10.2 mmol)
was stirred in toluene (250 mL) at reflux for 27 h. After cooling to room
temperature, sodium triacetoxyborohydride (3.74 g, 17.65 mmol) was added
and the mixture stirred for an additional 20 h. Water (100 mL) was added,
the organic layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with
EtOAc. The combined organic layers were concentrated and purified using
flash chromatography (CHCl3-5% MeOH/CHCl3) to yield the product as a
brown oil (5.56 g, >100%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 7.50 (d, J = 1.5
Hz, 1H), 7.44-7.33 (m, 6H), 7.09 (m, 6H), 6.26 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 4.6
(m, 1H), 4.25 (q, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 3.07 (bs, 1H), 3.20 (dd, J = 11, 17.6
Hz, 1H), 2.90 (q, J = 2.3 Hz, 2H), 2.70 (dd, J = 8.4, 17.6 Hz, 1H),
1.48-1.31 (m, 2H), 1.26 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.0 (m, 2H), 0.92-0.84 (m,
2H); MS (NH3-DCI) m/z 523 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isoxazolines as potent antagonists of the integrin αvβ3
