$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(2-(cis-3-(Piperidin-1-yl)cyclobutyl)benzothiazol-6-yl)pyridazin-3(2H)-one
(1): A mixture of 9 (3.75 kg, 12.6 mol, 1.0 equiv), pivalic acid (0.365
kg, 3.6 mol, 0.3 equiv), toluene (53 kg), and piperidine (1.6 kg, 18.6
mol, 1.5 equiv) was cooled under N2 to 5 °C. The toluene solution of
NaBH(OPiv)3 (15.3% w/w, 33.4 kg, 15.1 mol, 1.2 equiv) was added over 20
min. The reaction mixture was stirred at 5 °C for 16 h, at which time
HPLC analysis showed complete consumption of 9. The product was extracted
with 0.5 M sodium succinate solution buffered at pH 5.0 (60 kg, 2 x 28
kg). To the combined aqueous layers was added toluene (60 kg), and the pH
was adjusted to 9.7 using 50% NaOH (3.8 kg). The resulting two-layer
mixture was filtered through an in-line filter, and the lower aqueous
layer was removed and extracted with toluene (38 kg). The combined
organic layers were washed with water (39 kg), distilled to approximately
100 L, and transferred to a tared drum. This gave 72.5 kg of a light
yellow solution, whose concentration was determined to be 6.3% w/w of 1
by quantitative HPLC analysis versus an external standard. Yield 4.57 kg,
99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on reducing agent,
solvent, temperature, 98:2 Z:E
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Scalable Synthesis of a Cis-Substituted Cyclobutyl-Benzothiazole
Pyridazinone: Process Development of an Efficient Copper Catalyzed C-N
Cross-Coupling Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
