$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-{[1'-(1-Benzyl-1H-1,2,3-triazole-4-yl)ferrocene-1-yl]methyl}-4-(2-methoxyphenyl)piperazine
(13a). A solution of 12a (21.1 mg, 56.8 µmol),
1-(2-methoxyphenyl)piperazine (16.4 mg, 85.2 µmol), and Na(OAc)3BH(25.3
mg, 114 µmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (13 mL) was stirred at room temperature
overnight. The reaction mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried
(Na2SO4) and evaporated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
(CH2Cl2:MeOH 98:2) to give 13a as a yellow-orange solid (27.3 mg, 87%
yield);
1-(2-Methoxyphenyl)-4-{[1'-(1-pentyl-1H-1,2,3-triazole-4-yl)ferrocene-1-yl]methyl}piperazine
(13b). Compound 13b was prepared according to the protocol of 13a using a
solution of 12b (20.4 mg, 58.1 µmol), 1-(2-methoxyphenyl)piperazine (16.8
mg, 87.2 µmol), and Na(OAc)3BH (25.7 mg, 116 µmol) in CH2Cl2 (13 mL) to
give 13b as an orange-brown solid (30.4 mg, 99% yield); mp 92-94 °C. IR
2931, 2816, 1500, 1454, 1238, 1025, 748 cm-1. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3,) δ
0.92 (t, 3 H, J=6.99 Hz), 1.30-1.43 (m, 4 H), 1.94 (m, 2 H), 2.55 (m, 4
H), 3.02 (m, 4 H), 3.23 (s, 2 H), 3.83 (s, 3 H), 4.05 (m, 2 H), 4.10 (m,
2 H), 4.27 (m, 2 H), 4.35 (t, 2H, J=7.18 Hz), 4.68 (m, 2 H), 6.81-6.84
(m, 1 H), 6.86-6.90 (m, 2 H), 6.94-6.99 (m, 1 H), 7.44 (s, 1 H). 13C NMR
(150 MHz, CDCl3,) δ 13.90, 22.12, 28.66, 30.08, 50.29, 50.38, 52.74,
55.32, 57.65, 66.98, 69.14, 69.69, 71.80, 76.01, 82.97, 111.14, 118.21,
118.58, 120.96, 122.84, 141.32, 146.10, 152.24. HPLC system A (245 nm)
purity 97% (t R=16.9 min); system D (245 nm) purity >99% (t R=17.5 min).
HR-EIMS calcd m/z for C29H37FeN5O: 527.2348, found 527.2348.
