$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 107-06-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A vessel was charged with benzylamine (25.5 mL, 233 mmol, 1.0 equiv),
1,1-dimethoxypropan- 2-one (27.6 mL, 233 mmol 1.0 equiv), and DCE (819
mL). Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (69.2 g, 327 mmol, 1.40 equiv) was then
added in one portion and the reaction was aged overnight. GC analysis21
showed complete conversion and the reaction was diluted with a 2.5 w/w%
aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (700 mL) The resulting biphasic mixture was
mixed for 30 min. The organic layer was discarded and the aqueous layer
was basified by the addition of a 1 M NaOH aqueous solution to a pH of
∼14. The aqueous layer was then extracted with EtOAc (2 × 250 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with a 10 w/w% aqueous solution of
KH2PO4 to reach a pH of ∼7-8, and then washed with a 5 w/w% aqueous
solution of NaCl. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. N-benzyl-1,1-dimethoxypropan-2-amine
as a yellow oil (93% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM multikilogram scale
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
