$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
4-[3-(4-benzyl-piperzin-1-yl)-propoxy]-7-methoxy-3-phenyl-chromen-2-one
derivatives (7a-7f). A solution of
7-methoxy-3-phenyl-4-(3-piperzin-1-yl-pro-poxy)-chromen-2-one (6) (1 eq),
catalytic amount of acetic acid and different substituted aromatic
aldehydes (1.2 eq) in methanol (10 vol) was stirred for 3 h, (completion
of reaction evidenced by TLC) the reaction mixture cool to 0 °C slowly
added sodium cyano borohydride (1.5 eq). Then the reaction mixture wormed
to room temperature and for stirred again another 3-16 h. The completion
of reaction evidenced by TLC (absence of compound 6), the solvent was
evaporated by rotary, quenched with ice-cold water extracted with ethyl
acetate. The combined organic layers washed with water, brine solution
and dried over Na2SO4, concentrated under reduced pressure to afford
corresponding crude products, which on purification by flash
chromatography using 100-200 silica mesh to get the desire products
(7a-7f). The isolated products were confirmed by Mass, FT-IR and 1H NMR,
13C NMR and HRMS spectral analysis. Synthesis of
4-{3-[4-(4-propoxy-benzyl)-piperizin-1-yl]-propoxy}-7-methoxy-3-phenyl-2H-chromen-2-one
(7g). Yield 90 %, 18 h, thick liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz) in CDCl3: δ 1.04
(t, 3H, -OCH2 CH2 CH3); 1.80-1.74 (m, 4H, -CH2 propyl and -OCH2 CH2 CH3);
2.38 (t, 4H, Pipera-zine); 2.60 (t, 4H, Piperazine); 3.40 (t, 2H, -NCH2
pro-pyl); 3.78 (t, 2H, -OCH2 propyl); 3.95 (s, 5H,-OCH3 and -OCH2 CH2
CH3); 4.68 (s, 2H, -NCH2 Ar); 6.96 (d, 2H, Ar-H); 7.22 (d, 2H, Ar-H);
7.46-7.32 (m, 5H, Ar-H); 7.53 (d, 2H, Ar-H); 7.68 (s, 1H, Ar-H); 13C NMR
in CDCl3 (75 MHz): δ 166.98, 161.32, 156.78, 152.26, 148.86, 134.65,
132.10, 128.78, 126.24, 115.25, 112.62, 109.24, 107.78, 74.43, 60.34,
58.80, 55.08, 52.12, 30.61, 26.98, 22.70, 12.02; MS m/z: 543 (M+H)+ +ve
scan.
