$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N-Butyl-L-ido-1-deoxynojirimycin (15).
Butyraldehyde (66 μL, 0.73 mmol) and NaCNBH3 (27 mg, 0.44 mmol) were
successively added to a solution of 13 (76 mg, 0.145 mmol) in CH3CN/AcOH
(1.45 mL, 30/1, v/v). The reaction mixture was stirred for 20 hours after
which sat. aq. NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added and the resulting mixture was
extracted with Et2O (3×5 mL). The combined organic phases were dried
(Na2SO4) and concentrated to provide the crude N-butylated intermediate
(Rf = 0.5 in 4:1; PE:EtOAc). The crude intermediate was coevaporated with
dichloroethane and dissolved in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL). The solution was cooled
to 0°C and BCl3 (1.74 mL, 1M in CH2Cl2) was added. After stirring for 20
hours at 0°C MeOH (2 mL) was carefully added. The mixture was
concentrated and coevaporated with toluene. The residue was purified by
flash silica gel chromatography (0→ MeOH in CHCl3 + 1% NH4OH) to produce
15 (26 mg, 0.12 mmol) in 82% yield over two steps as a colorless oil.
N-[5-(Adamantan-1-yl-methoxy)-pentyl]-L-altro-1-deoxynojirimycin (29).
Compound 29 (34 mg, 85 μmol) was synthesized from 26 (50 mg, 96 μmol) in
89% yield as a colorless oil following the reductive amination procedure
as described for 15, but now with 5-(adamantane-1-yl-methoxy)-1-pentanal
1621 (48 mg, 0.19 mmol) and the deprotection procedure as described for
4. Flash silica gel chromatography (0→ OH in CHCl3 + 1% NH4OH). Rf
N-alkylated intermediate = 0.60 (4:1; PE:EtOAc); Rf 29 = 0.27 (3:1;
EtOAc:MeOH + 1% NH4OH). 1H NMR (400 MHz, MeOD) δ 4.21 (dd, J = 2.7, 4.8,
1H, H-3), 4.11 - 4.07 (m, 1H, H-2), 4.03 - 3.98 (m, 1H, H-5), 3.76 (d, J
= 5.3, 2H, CH2-6), 3.59 (dd, J = 5.1, 11.1, 1H, H-1a), 3.40 (t, J = 6.3,
2H, OCH2-5' pentyl), 3.15 - 3.10 (m, 1H, H-4), 3.10 - 3.02 (m, 1H,
NCHH-1' pentyl), 2.97 (s, 2H, OCH2), 2.64-2.58 (m, 2H, H-1b, NCHH-1'
pentyl), 1.95 (s, 3H, 3×CH adamantane), 1.79 - 1.67 (m, 6H, 3×CH2
adamantane), 1.66 - 1.58 (m, 4H, CH2-2' CH2-4' pentyl), 1.56 (d, J = 2.5,
6H, 3×CH2 adamantane,), 1.46 - 1.38 (m, 2H, CH2-3' pentyl). 13C NMR (75
MHz, D2O) δ 83.2 (OCH2), 79.2 (C-3), 76.8 (C-2), 72.5 (OCH2-5' pentyl),
71.3 (C-5), 69.6 (C-4), 65.3 (C-6), 60.0 (C-1), 57.7 (NCH2-1' pentyl),
41.0 (3×CH2adamantane), 38.5 (3×CH2 adamantane), 35.3 (Cq adamantane),
30.6 (CH2-4' pentyl), 29.9 (3×CH adamantane), 28.2 (CH2-2' pentyl), 25.1
(CH2-3' pentyl). IR νmax(thin film)/ cm-1: 3360, 2902, 2849, 1652, 1452,
1110. [α]20D: -28.8 (c 0.3, CH3OH). HRMS: found 398.2888 [M+H]+,
calculated for [C22H39O5N1+H]+ 398.2901.
