$DATUM N-Benzyloxyethyl-1-deoxynojirimycin (9). 2-(Benzyloxy)-acetaldehyde (1.18
mL, 8.4 mmol) and NaCNBH3 (703 mg, 11.2 mmol) were successively added toa
solution of the HCl salt of 1-deoxynojirimycin (8) (1.125 g, 5.6 mmol) in
MeOH/AcOH (56 mL, 150/1 v/v). The resulting solution was stirred for 48
hours and subsequently the pH was adjusted to 8 with saturated aq. 1M
NaOH. The reaction mixture was concentrated and coevaporated with
toluene. The residue was dissolved in methanol, celite was added, and the
resulting suspension was concentrated and purified on a silicagel column
(0→ MeOH in CHCl3 + 1% NH4OH) to produce 9 (1.431 g, 4.8 mmol) in 86%
yield as a white foam. N-Benzyloxyethyl-1-deoxynojirimycin (9), yield
1.431 g, 4.8 mmol, 86% Rf = 0.15 (1:4; MeOH:CHCl3 +0.5% NH4OH). 1H NMR
(200 MHz, MeOD) δ 7.43 - 7.11 (m, 5H), 4.51 (s, 2H), 3.93 (dd, J = 1.9,
12.0, 1H), 3.83 (dd, J = 1.7, 12.1, 1H), 3.61 (t, J = 5.2, 2H), 3.54 -
3.33 (m, 2H), 3.25 - 2.98 (m, 3H), 2.74 (dt, J = 4.7, 14.4, 1H), 2.39 -
2.14 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, MeOD) δ 137.8, 129.2, 128.9, 128.8, 78.2,
73.3, 69.8, 68.7, 66.1, 66.0, 57.2, 56.1, 51.5. IR νmax(thin film)/ cm-1:
3341, 2955, 2716, 1636, 1458, 1396, 1366, 1080, 1026, 748. [αD: -0.6 (c
3.2, MeOH). HRMS: found 298.1664 [M+H]+, calculated for [C15H23O5N1+H]+
298.1649.
