$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Butyl-L-ido-1-deoxynojirimycin (15). Butyraldehyde (66 μL, 0.73 mmol)
and NaCNBH3 (27 mg, 0.44 mmol) were successively added to a solution of
13 (76 mg, 0.145 mmol) in CH3CN/AcOH (1.45 mL, 30/1, v/v). The reaction
mixture was stirred for 20 hours after which sat. aq. NaHCO3 (5 mL) was
added and the resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (3×5 mL). The
combined organic phases were dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated to provide
the crude N-butylated intermediate (Rf = 0.5 in 4:1; PE:EtOAc). The crude
intermediate was coevaporated with dichloroethane and dissolved in CH2Cl2
(1.5 mL). The solution was cooled to 0°C and BCl3 (1.74 mL, 1M in CH2Cl2)
was added. After stirring for 20 hours at 0°C MeOH (2 mL) was carefully
added. The mixture was concentrated and coevaporated with toluene. The
residue was purified by flash silica gel chromatography (0→ MeOH in CHCl3
+ 1% NH4OH) to produce 15 (26 mg, 0.12 mmol) in 82% yield over two steps
as a colorless oil. N-Butyl-L-ido-1-deoxynojirimycin (15), yield 26 mg,
0.12 mmol, 82% Rf = 0.18 (3:1; CHCl3:MeOH + 1% NH4OH). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
MeOD) δ 4.06 - 3.96 (m, 3H, CH2-6, H-4), 3.94 (d, J = 7.4, 1H, H-2), 3.83
(s, 1H, H-3), 3.51 (s, 1H, H-5), 3.44 (d, J = 12.8, 1H, H-1a), 3.36 -
3.28 (m, 3H, H-1b, CH2-1'), 1.87 - 1.65 (m, 2H, CH2-2'), 1.48 - 1.38 (m,
2H, CH2-3'), 1.01 (t, J = 7.4, 3H, CH3-4'). 13C NMR (100 MHz,MeOD) δ
69.2, 63.8, 55.0, 21.1 (CH2-3'), 14.1 (CH3-4'). IR νmax(thin film)/ cm-1:
3279, 2963, 2876, 1637, 1653, 1445, 1063, 979.4. [α]20D: +12.2 (c 0.7,
CH3OH). HRMS: found 220.1538 [M+H]+, calculated for [C10H21O4N1+H]+
220.1543.
