$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To verify the structure of the byproduct, Cbz-deprotected (R)-9 was
converted to the corresponding ethylated product in 76% yield via
reductive amination using acetaldehyde and NaBH(OAc)3 (reaction not
shown). The NMR spectra of the synthesized compound and that of
(R)-LLpipEtG (11) were identical. Analytical reversed phase HPLC (the
mobile phase was 10.8-37.2% CH3CN in H2O for 30 min, with 0.1% TFA
throughout) tR 7.1 min, 100% purity; 1H NMR (CD3OD) δ 4.92-4.83 (m, 1H,
), 4.78 (app d, 1H), 4.47-4.32 (m, 1H), 4.16-3.88 (m, 3H), 3.44-3.26 (m,
3H), 3.15 (app t, 1H), 2.85 (app t, 1H), 2.71-2.58 (m, 1H) 2.29-2.14 (m,
1H), 2.05-1.88 (m, 1H), 1.87-1.56 (m, 6H), 1.55-1.40 (m, 1H), 1.39-1.25
(t, 3H), 1.06-0.85 (m, 12H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CD3OD) δ 173.2, 171.0,
168.5, 61.8, 52.9, 52.0, 50.9, 49.6, 46.8, 43.2, 41.8, 41.5, 25.9, 25.8,
25.3, 23.5, 23.2 (2C), 22.0, 21.7, 9.9; [α]D 20 -15.2 (c 1.0, CH3OH); IR
(KBr) v 3444, 2364, 1683, 1540, 1201 cm-1; HRMS (FT-ICR-MS) Calcd for
C21H41N5O3 [M+H]+ 412.3280, found 412.3282.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternate preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 3-Aminopiperidine-based peptide analogues as the first selective
noncovalent inhibitors of the bacterial cysteine protease IdeS
